From e1bb6df2aa8ddf2255d24389c2533e0620a4e3ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:31:58 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18h: route client certificate selection to the
 host

Registry tabs hand ChromeContentBrowserClient::SelectClientCertificate's identity list and ClientCertificateDelegate to a bounded host request/response channel after Chromium's enterprise auto-select policy runs. The host sees challenger origin plus per-identity subject, issuer, expiry and SHA-256 leaf fingerprint, never key or certificate bytes. A listed fingerprint acquires the private key asynchronously through SelfOwningAcquirePrivateKey; cancel, no callback, navigation, close, replacement, 30-second deadline and SSL-handler cancellation drop the delegate (abort, never a cached no-certificate choice), including while acquisition is in flight. Error-page auto-reload no longer retries ERR_SSL_CLIENT_AUTH_CERT_NEEDED, which would re-ask after every abort. A test-only memory ClientCertStore over net/data identities exists only in !NDEBUG non-official builds and only with --rearc-test-client-cert-dir plus --use-mock-keychain in embedded mode; no Keychain identity is read. ABI 1.41 / bridge 0.43.0 (client_certificates); loopback mutual-TLS selection, cancel, invalid fingerprint, cache, navigation/close/acquisition/signing/replacement/shutdown cases pass with no outside connection.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
